%
(=======================================================================)
(                     RRRRRR    EEEEEEEE  BBBBBBB                       )
(                     RR   RR   EE        BB    BB                      )
(                     RR   RR   EE        BB    BB                      )
(                     RRRRRR    EEEEEE    BBBBBBB                       )
(                     RR   RR   EE        BB    BB                      )
(                     RR    RR  EE        BB    BB                      )
(                     RR    RR  EEEEEEEE  BBBBBBB                       )
(                                                                       )
( Rose Engine Butler                                                    )
(=======================================================================)
( BASKET WEAVE PATTERN                                                  )
(=======================================================================)
( Version 1.1, 17 August 2026, R. Colvin                                )
(=======================================================================)
( Gcode for use on a rose engine using the Rose Engine Butler           )
( configuration of LinuxCNC.                                            )
(                                                                       )
( Licensing for the use of this program are at the bottom of this file. )
(=======================================================================)
(  *** OPERATOR NOTE ***                                                )
(  The Rose Engine Butler configuration of LinuxCNC will need to have   )
(  these axis selections:                                               )
(     - C                                                               )
(     - Z                                                               )
(     - either X or U                                                   )
(=======================================================================)
(  CHECK THESE BEFORE RUNNING                                           )

(-- USER PARAMETERS - PATTERN ------------------------------------------)
(   Ensure the USER PARAMETERS below are good values for your           )
(   desired pattern and machine.                                        ) 

#1 = 02.000                          (Diameter of piece in inches.  If  )
                                     ( machine setup is using G21, then )
                                     (this is in mm.                    )
#2 = 24                              (Number of Waves - number of boxes )
                                     (around perimeter                  )
#3 = 3                               (Number of CutsPerWave, typ. 3 or 4)
#4 = 2                               (Rows of Patterns                  )

(=======================================================================)
(   CUTTER PLUNGE OPTION                                                )
(   The X axis can be used for plunging the cutter into the workpiece   )
(   for cutting, and then withdrawing it when the cutter needs to be    )
(   repositioned.                                                       )
(        -X = engage cutter                                             )
(        +X = withdraw cutter                                           )
(                                                                       )
(   Alternatively, the retractor can be used to move the headstock away )
(   from the cutter -- i.e., withdrawing the cutter, or into the cutter )
(   -- i.e., engaging the cutter.  The retractor is setup in this code  )
(   as the U axis.                                                      )
(        +U = move headstock into cutter - engage the cutter            )
(        -U = move headstock away from cutter - withdraw the cutter     )
(                                                                       )
(   In either case, the Z axis is used with the Spindle to move the     )
(   cutter whilst cutting.                                              )

#10 = 2                              (Cutter plunge option              )
                                     (   1 = Use X axis                 )
                                     (   2 = Use U axis                 )

(=======================================================================)
(   X/U AXIS PARAMETERS                                                 )
(   The X axis is used to plunge the cutter into the workpiece, and     )
(   withdraw it from the piece between repositioning moves.             )
(                                                                       )
(   Starting position for X is at the withdrawn position, so that when  )
(   plunged to #22 distance, it is at the desired depth. Be sure to     )
(   account for backlash.                                               )
(                                                                       )
(   Starting position for U is at the headstock pushed away position,   )
(   so that when plunged to #22 distance, it is at the desired depth.   )
(   Be sure to account for backlash.                                    )

#20 = 10.000                         (Feed rate for withdraw,           )
                                     (in/min or mm/min                  )
#21 =  1.000                         (Feed rate for plunge,             )
                                     (in/min or mm/min                  )
#22 =  0.500                         (Distance to plunge/withdraw,      )
                                     (in or mm                          )

(=======================================================================)
(   C AXIS PARAMETERS                                                   )
(   Set the start position for C so that it is where you wish to begin  )
(   cutting the pattern.  Be sure to account for backlash.              )
(                                                                       )
(   Check that the scale for the C axis is appropriately set. This is   ) 
(   set in Rose Engine Butler on the Settings screen.                   )
(                                                                       )
(   Check that backlash for this axis is set appropriately. This is     ) 
(   set in Rose Engine Butler on the Settings screen.                   )

#30 = 600.00    (Feed, C reposition move, in/min or mm/min              )

(=======================================================================)
(   Z AXIS PARAMETERS                                                   )
(   Set the start position for Z so that it is where you wish to begin  )
(   cutting the pattern.  Be sure to account for backlash.              )
(                                                                       )
(   Check that the scale for the Z axis is appropriately set. This is   ) 
(   set in Rose Engine Butler on the Settings screen.                   )
(                                                                       )
(   Check that backlash for this axis is set appropriately. This is     ) 
(   set in Rose Engine Butler on the Settings screen.                   )

#40 = 02.00                          (Feed, Z reposition move,          )
                                     (in/min or mm/min                  )

(=======================================================================)
(   C & Z AXES - SYNCHRONIZED MOVEMENT PARAMETERS                       )

#50 = 10.00                          (Feed, synchronized cutting move,  )
                                     (in/min or mm/min                  )
#51 = 02.00                          (Feed, repositioning move,         )
                                     (in/min or mm/min                  )

(=======================================================================)
(   OTHER PARAMETERS                                                    )
(-- Starting side for cutting the pattern                               )
#60 = 1                              (Starting side                     )
                                     (   1 = left; headstock side,      )
                                     (       moving towards tailstock   )
                                     (   2 = right; tailstock side,     )
                                     (       moving towards headstock   )

(=======================================================================)
( PROGRAM FOR MAKING THIS PATTERN FOLLOWS.  CHANGES ARE NOT RECOMMENDED.)
(=======================================================================)
(-- CONSTANTS ----------------------------------------------------------)
#90 = 3.14159265                         (Pi                            )

(=======================================================================)
(-- CALCULATED VALUES --------------------------------------------------)
#101 = [#1 / 2]                      (Piece's radius, inch or mm        )
#102 = [[360 / #2] / 2]              (Spindle Amplitude, deg            )
#103 = [#101 * #102 * [#90 / 180]]   (Z Amplitude = chord length for    )
                                     (Spindle Amplitude, inch or mm     )
                                        
(-- CALCULATED VALUES - REPOSITIONING FOR NEXT CUT IN WAVE -------------)
#104 = [#102 / #3]                   (Spindle / C axis                  )
O01 IF [#60 EQ 1]                    (Z axis                            )
  #105 = [#103 / #3]                 (Move away from headstock          )
O01 ELSE
  #105 = [-#103 / #3]                (Move towards headstock            )
O01 ENDIF

(-- CALCULATED VALUES - REPOSITIONING FOR NEXT WAVE --------------------)
#106 = [#104 * [#3 - 1]]             (Spindle / C axis                  )
#107 = [#105 * [#3 - 1]]             (Z axis                            )

(=======================================================================)
(-- MACHINE / MODE SETUP -----------------------------------------------)
G20                                  (Imperial mode / G21 is metric     )
G91                                  (Use incremental mode for all      )
                                     (pattern moves below               )

(=======================================================================)
(-- Loop: repeat number of Rows of Patterns times ----------------------)
#501 = 1
O02 WHILE [#501 LT [#4 + 1]]

  (-- Loop: repeat number Cuts Per Wave --------------------------------)
  #502 = 1
  O021 WHILE [#502 LT [#3 + 1]]
  
    (-- Plunge the cutter into the workpiece ---------------------------)
    O0211 IF [#10 EQ 1]              (Use the X axis for plunging       )
      G1 X[-#22] F#21                (Plunge cutter into piece          )
    O0211 ELSE                       (Use the retractor for plunging    )
      G1 U[#22] F#21                 (Release the headstock = plunge    )
                                     (cutter into piece                 )
    O0211 ENDIF

    (-- O03 Loop: repeat number Waves ----------------------------------)
    #503 = 1
    O0212 WHILE [#503 LT [#2 + 1]]
      O02121 IF [#60 EQ 1]           (Starting on the headstock side    )
        G1 C#102 Z[#103] F#50
        G1 C#102 Z[-#103] F#50
      O02121 ELSE                    (Starting on the tailstock side    )
        G1 C#102 Z[-#103] F#50
        G1 C#102 Z[#103] F#50
      O02121 ENDIF
      #503 = [#503 + 1]
    O0212 ENDWHILE
          
    (-- Withdraw the cutter from the workpiece -------------------------)
    O0213 IF [#10 EQ 1]              (Use the X axis for withdrawing    )
                                     (the cutter                        )
      G1 X[#22] F#20                 (Withdraw cutter                   )
    O0213 ELSE                       (Use the retractor for             )
                                     (withdrawing the cutter            )
      G1 U[-#22] F#20                (Push the headstock towards the    )
                                     (back = withdraw the cutter        )
    O0213 ENDIF

    (-- If not the last pass, re-position the cutter for the next Cut --)
    (-- in the Wave ----------------------------------------------------)
    O0214 IF [#502 LT #3]
      O02141 IF [#60 EQ 1]           (Starting on the headstock side    )
        G1 C#106 Z[-#107] F#51
      O02141 ELSE                    (Starting on the tailstock side    )
        G1 C#106 Z[#107] F#51
      O02141 ENDIF
    O0214 ENDIF
    #502 = [#502 + 1]
  O021 ENDWHILE

  #104 = [-#104]  (Reverse spindle repositioning per cut per wave)
  #501 = [#501 + 1]
O02 ENDWHILE

(-- PROGRAM END --------------------------------------------------------)
M2
